The eight-Spark configuration uses native CUDA-resident Engram shards,
without the NVMe row-store hook or TP3 padding. It adds source-identity
checks, launch/distribution tooling, and capability/numerical validation.
The retained experimental admission hook is disabled in EP4; the active
scheduler setting is --min-free-slots-delay 1.

SGLang, FlashInfer, PyTorch, NVIDIA components and DeepSeek model weights
retain their own licenses. No model weights, credentials, or prebuilt
container image are redistributed here. Product names identify upstream
products; no affiliation or endorsement is implied.

EP4/SG5 changes the routed-expert partition to EP4/MoE-TP2 while retaining
global TP8. The local DSpark worker change wraps draft lifecycle operations
in the existing speculative backend context and records actual methods and
shapes. Its SGLang-derived source remains Apache-2.0. The numerical
validation/reference source files are unmodified pinned SGLang fixtures
under Apache-2.0; they are not applied as production overlays.

